</solution></exercise>
</example>
<para>What patterns do you notice? Can you use those ideas to find the vertices for the next equation? What do you know about whether it will open up or down?</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="e97a365f-1e27-4b93-bd6d-96a10e2e7517" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>Without graphing, find the coordinates of the vertex of \(y=-(x−4)^2+8\) and determine if it opens up or down.</para>
      <para> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 4.</para><para>The correct answer is is 4. The x-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 4.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="cc967510-ac1e-4d56-9e53-cfdeb3d963a6" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 8.</para><para>The correct answer is is 8. The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 8.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="82feb2b3-eeb0-4f87-a8d9-d9ec880ba7e9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> Does the graph open up or down?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The graph opens downward. The squared term has a negative coefficient (-1).</para><para>Incorrect. The correct answer is Down. The graph opens downward. The squared term has a negative coefficient (-1).</para></solution></exercise></section>
