<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="b7ffe64f-8102-4a51-9f6f-84b79dbfdc7e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>The next equation, \(y=x^2−7\), looks a little different from the previous ones. Can you use what you’ve learned to find the coordinates of its vertex and determine if it opens up or down.</para>
      <para> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 0.</para><para>The correct answer is is 0. The x-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 0.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="063d8b56-a3bd-4556-aef6-27009f2924b7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is -7.</para><para>The correct answer is is -7. The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is -7.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="1784d2b5-6e56-46d5-bb4f-108a5d865091" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> Does the graph open up or down?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient \((1)\).</para><para>Incorrect. The correct answer is Up.The graph opens upward. The squared term has a positive coefficient \((1)\).</para></solution></exercise></section><example><exercise>
