<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="06c86bbb-e9b6-4927-8751-95ce8e76aef4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>Use the completed rows of the table to hypothesize about the coordinates of the vertex of the equation in the last row, and whether the parabola opens up or down.</para>
      <para> For the equation \(y=a(x+m)^2+n\), what is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is –\(m\).</para><para>The correct answer is is –\(m\). The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is –\(m\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="8e9f2598-2017-457c-bd50-9015f7ebfbb7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para> For the equation \(y=a(x+m)^2+n\), what is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(n\).</para><para>The correct answer is is \(n\). The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(n\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="10468be6-f473-420b-b5a3-b14329156584" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> For the equation \(y=a(x+m)^2+n\), can you determine if the graph opens up or down with the information you are given? </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! No, because the direction of opening depends on whether \(a\) is positive or negative.</para><para>Incorrect. No, because the direction of opening depends on whether \(a\) is positive or negative.</para></solution></exercise></section>
